{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Extend the Universal Credit Holiday Limit from 28 Days to 40 Days",
        "additional_details": "The Government must modernise these rules to reflect the realities of modern family life. Universal Credit should not punish people for doing the right thing in a family crisis. No claimant should be forced to choose between standing by a loved one in an emergency and keeping the support they need to pay for rent, food, and basic living costs.",
        "background": "Many Universal Credit claimants have close family living overseas.They may need to visit elderly parents, care for a seriously ill relative,attend funeral, settle family matters,or support loved ones during a crisis. These situations are often unexpected and cannot always be resolved within 28 days.",
